>> title: Risotto alla Milanese
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: rice, saffron, italian, stovetop
>> servings: 4
>> time: 40 min
>> step.1: steep
>> step.2: sweat 6 min
>> step.3: toast 2 min, deglaze
>> step.4: ladle in, stir 18 min
>> step.5: beat in off the heat

Steep @saffron threads{1/4%tsp}(a large pinch, crumbled) in @beef stock{6%cups}(1.4 L; kept hot).

Sweat @yellow onion{1%small}(finely chopped) and @beef marrow{2%Tbs}(optional, but traditional) in @unsalted butter{3%Tbs} in a #wide saucepan{} for ~{6%min}.

Toast @Arborio rice{1 1/2%cups}(300 g) in @&(~1)onion{} for ~{2%min}, then deglaze with @dry white wine{1/2%cup}(120 mL).

Add @&(~3)saffron stock{} to @&(~1)rice{} a ladleful at a time, stirring, until the grains are al dente, ~{18%min}.

Beat @grated Parmesan{3/4%cup}(65 g), @cold unsalted butter{2%Tbs}, and @kosher salt{1%tsp} into @&(~1)risotto{} off the heat.
